{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"ls -la /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16 && rg -n \\\"\\\" /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16 -g '*'\"","aggregated_output":"total 52\ndrwxrwxr-x+  2 xd xd  4096 May 26 00:34 .\ndrwxrwxr-x+ 19 xd xd  4096 May 25 23:39 ..\n-rw-rw-r--+  1 xd xd 10507 May 26 00:34 des.md\n-rw-rw-r--+  1 xd xd   295 May 25 23:39 ids.txt\n-rw-rw-r--+  1 xd xd 24662 May 25 23:39 prompt.md\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:1:你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:2:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:3:每个参考题描述包含：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:4:- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:5:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:6:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:7:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:8:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:9:参考题目如下：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:10:<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"de809cff\" lines=\"86-103\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:11:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:12:Turn black dents in two colored regions into marked opposite-color patches.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:13:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:14:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:15:- Black background with two large foreground colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:16:- The large regions contain small black dents and a few one-cell color specks\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:17:  or protrusions along region boundaries.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:18:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:19:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:20:- Locally clean the two foreground regions: isolated specks become black, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:21:  one-cell protrusions surrounded by the other region take that region's color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:22:- Each original black dent whose cleaned 3x3 neighborhood is mostly one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:23:  foreground color becomes the center of a 3x3 patch in the opposite color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:24:- The dent center itself is recolored teal (8).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:25:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:26:Key insight: The teal pixels mark the original black defects; the surrounding\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:27:3x3 patch uses the other foreground color, after first removing boundary noise.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:28:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:29:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:30:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:31:<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"b25e450b\" lines=\"28-43\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:32:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:33:Slide each black border rectangle to the opposite border, recoloring its swept stripe orange and leaving the rectangle black at the far edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:34:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:35:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:36:- The grid contains black rectangular 4-connected masks, each touching exactly one outer border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:37:- Grey cells form incidental pattern content; orange is the trail color used when a black mask slides.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:38:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:39:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:40:- Treat all black rectangles as moving simultaneously.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:41:- A rectangle touching the top or bottom edge moves vertically to the opposite edge in the same columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:42:- A rectangle touching the left or right edge moves horizontally to the opposite edge in the same rows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:43:- Recolor the complete swept row or column stripe to orange, then stamp every destination rectangle in black.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:44:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:45:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:46:- Edge contact gives the slide direction; the output is the set of opposite-edge black rectangles plus their orange trails.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:47:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:48:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:49:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:50:<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"31f7f899\" lines=\"7-21\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:51:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:52:Sort vertical bars by height and redistribute them across fixed colored slots.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:53:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:54:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:55:- bg background; a horizontal base line of a single color spans the full grid width.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:56:- Several monochrome vertical bars of distinct colors rise upward from the base line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:57:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:58:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:59:- Rank bar shapes by height (shortest to tallest).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:60:- Rank original x-positions (slots) left to right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:61:- Place the i-th shortest shape into the i-th leftmost slot, recoloring it to that slot's original color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:62:- The base line is preserved unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:63:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:64:Key insight: Each slot keeps its x-position and color identity; only the bar silhouettes are redistributed among slots by height order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:65:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:66:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:67:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:68:<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"a2d730bd\" lines=\"43-56\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:69:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:70:Extend each solid foreground rectangle toward its same-color isolated pixels with capped one-cell paths, clearing each original marker pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:71:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:72:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:73:- The background is the dominant color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:74:- Each foreground color has exactly one solid rectangular object and one or more isolated same-color marker pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:75:- Every marker is horizontally or vertically aligned with the rectangle bbox and lies outside it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:76:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:77:- For each marker, draw a one-cell-wide straight path from the adjacent side of the rectangle through one cell beyond the marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:78:- Add a three-pixel perpendicular cap at the rectangle end and around the marker endpoint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:79:- Recolor the original marker pixel to background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:80:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:81:- The isolated pixels are not copied; they mark the hollow endpoints of capped protrusions grown from their matching rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:82:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:83:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:84:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:85:<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"17829a00\" lines=\"21-36\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:86:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:87:Move each colored object vertically until it touches the matching top or bottom border bar.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:88:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:89:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:90:- The background is the dominant color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:91:- The top row is a full-width bar in one foreground color and the bottom row is a full-width bar in another.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:92:- All other foreground pixels are 8-connected monochrome objects whose color matches one of those bars.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:93:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:94:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:95:- Top-bar-colored objects move upward so their bbox top is row 1.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:96:- Bottom-bar-colored objects move downward so their bbox bottom is the row above the bottom bar.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:97:- A downward-moving one-column segment whose landing overlaps its source becomes the continuous vertical segment swept between them.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:98:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:99:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:100:The horizontal bars are destination anchors: color determines which border an object slides toward, while columns and object shape are otherwise preserved.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:101:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:102:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:103:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:104:<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"aaecdb9a\" lines=\"10-26\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:105:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:106:Convert scattered foreground objects into bottom-aligned count bars in a fixed five-color order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:107:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:108:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:109:The grid has a dominant background color and foreground objects in the task\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:110:palette: grey, red, teal, maroon, and pink. Objects are monochromatic\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:111:8-connected components; some palette colors may be absent.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:112:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:113:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:114:For each palette color in order grey, red, teal, maroon, pink, count its\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:115:8-connected objects. Create a background grid with five columns and height\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:116:equal to the largest count, then fill each column upward from the bottom\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:117:with its palette color for that count.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:118:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:119:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:120:The output does not preserve object shapes or positions; it is a histogram\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:121:of per-color 8-connected object counts, using the learned palette order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:122:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:123:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:124:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:125:<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"f0f8a26d\" lines=\"30-44\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:126:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:127:Rotate every foreground bar 90 degrees around its own center on the same canvas.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:128:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:129:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:130:The background is the dominant color, and all foreground pixels share one color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:131:Each 4-connected foreground object is a solid one-cell-thick horizontal or vertical\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:132:bar with odd length, with single-pixel bars allowed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:133:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:134:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:135:Clear the canvas to the background, then redraw every bar with its midpoint, length,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:136:and color preserved while swapping horizontal and vertical orientation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:137:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:138:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:139:The bars are independent objects: their centers and lengths identify the output\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:140:placement, so no matching, ordering, or global symmetry is needed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:141:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:142:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:143:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:144:<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"6cbe9eb8\" lines=\"79-94\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:145:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:146:Rebuild the foreground rectangles as a largest-to-smallest lower-left nesting.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:147:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:148:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:149:- A periodic wallpaper background is overlaid by foreground colors that each form a rectangular frame or solid rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:150:- The largest foreground rectangle is the output frame; smaller foreground rectangles are the objects to nest inside it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:151:- A frame may be partially hidden by a smaller rectangle, but its visible pixels still determine its bbox.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:152:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:153:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:154:- Ignore the wallpaper and crop the result to the largest foreground rectangle's bbox size.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:155:- Sort foreground rectangles by bbox area from largest to smallest.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:156:- Reconstruct each frame or solid rectangle, placing every next smaller rectangle in the lower-left of the current rectangle's usable region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:157:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:158:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:159:- The scattered background colors are not objects; the meaningful order is the unique descending rectangle size chain, and each step nests into the previous rectangle's lower-left interior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:160:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:161:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:162:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:163:<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"1ae2feb7\" lines=\"30-45\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:164:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:165:Extend row bars periodically across the opposite side of a separator column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:166:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:167:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:168:- bg = background. A near-solid vertical separator divides the grid into two sides.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:169:- One side contains horizontal colored bars; the other side is blank target space.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:170:- Bars may be stacked by row and may sit at different distances from the separator.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:171:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:172:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:173:- Identify the separator as the column whose non-bg cells are one color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:174:- Treat the denser side as the bar side and collect each contiguous row run.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:175:- Process bars from nearest to farthest from the separator; for each bar, paint its\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:176:  color every bar-length cells into the blank side without overwriting earlier paint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:177:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:178:Key insight: Each bar's length is the period for its extension, and nearer bars claim target cells first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:179:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:180:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:181:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:182:<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"247ef758\" lines=\"35-46\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:183:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:184:Move colored sprites from the left strip into a framed area at marker-defined targets.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:185:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:186:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:187:- bg background; rectangular frame on right with colored markers on its edges; sprites in a narrow left strip separated by a constant-color divider column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:188:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:189:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:190:- For each color, target rows/cols are where both opposite frame edges share that color. Targets are the Cartesian product.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:191:- Erase each sprite from the left and stamp it centered at every target. Higher sprites cover lower ones.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:192:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:193:Key insight: One sprite replicates to a grid of row × column marker intersections.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:194:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:195:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:196:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:197:<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"9caf5b84\" lines=\"28-45\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:198:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:199:Recolor every pixel whose color is not one of the two most frequent input colors to orange.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:200:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:201:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:202:- The grid contains at least three colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:203:- Orange is absent from the input and is used only as the output replacement color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:204:- Exactly two colors occupy the top two frequency ranks; they may tie with each\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:205:  other, but no third color ties them at the cutoff.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:206:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:207:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:208:- Preserve every pixel whose color is one of the two most frequent input colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:209:- Replace every other pixel with orange.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:210:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:211:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:212:- The visible distinction is not the numeric identity of the colors but their\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:213:  population: the two majority colors remain, while all minority colors merge\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:214:  into the new orange color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:215:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:216:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:217:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:218:<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5587a8d0\" lines=\"11-27\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:219:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:220:Redraw foreground objects as nested square rings ordered by object size.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:221:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:222:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:223:- The grid has one dominant background color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:224:- Every foreground object is a 4-connected monochromatic component.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:225:- Foreground object areas are distinct.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:226:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:227:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:228:- Sort the foreground objects by decreasing pixel count.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:229:- Create a square output with side length 2 * number_of_objects - 1.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:230:- The largest object color fills the outer ring, each next object color fills\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:231:  the next inner ring, and the smallest object color fills the center pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:232:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:233:Key insight: The objects' original shapes do not get copied; their areas\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:234:determine only the outside-to-inside order of the nested square pattern.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:235:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:236:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:237:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:238:<reference_puzzle index=\"13\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"db7260a4\" lines=\"37-56\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:239:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:240:Drop the singleton marker into the matching red U-shaped container, or make a bottom-row puddle if no closed container is hit.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:241:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:242:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:243:- The grid has a dominant background, one singleton marker pixel on the top row,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:244:  and one other foreground color forming vertical bars and bottom segments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:245:- A closed container is a U shape: two vertical side bars with a continuous\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:246:  bottom segment between them and an empty rectangular interior above the bottom.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:247:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:248:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:249:- Remove the top marker from its original cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:250:- If exactly one closed U-shaped container has the marker column within its\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:251:  horizontal footprint, fill that container's empty interior with the marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:252:- If no closed container is under the marker column, fill the whole bottom row\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:253:  with the marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:254:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:255:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:256:- The marker does not identify a color by value; it identifies a vertical drop\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:257:  column, and only a structurally closed U shape can catch and contain the fill.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:258:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:259:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:260:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:261:<reference_puzzle index=\"14\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"88bcf3b4\" lines=\"229-241\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:262:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:263:Swing an irregular line segment around a nearby obstacle sprite, preserving its pixel count.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:264:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:265:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:266:- bg, bar color (straight lines perpendicular to the grid edge, one end on the border), segment color (irregular stroke attached to bar's inner endpoint), obstacle color (sprite near the bar terminal).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:267:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:268:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:269:- Each bar is perpendicular to the edge it touches; its inner (terminal) endpoint has an attached irregular segment.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:270:- The segment detaches and re-routes: it travels from the terminal toward the nearest obstacle, hugs the obstacle's boundary, then exits at a 45° diagonal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:271:- Total painted pixels equal the original segment length.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:272:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:273:Key insight: The segment behaves like a rope swung around the obstacle — attach at the nearest point, trace the skin, exit diagonally, conserving length.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:274:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:275:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:276:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:277:<reference_puzzle index=\"15\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"984d8a3e\" lines=\"5-21\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:278:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:279:Shift each row's dominant middle-color run left until its right edge aligns with the leftmost original right edge, moving displaced left-side pixels after the run.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:280:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:281:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:282:- The grid has three colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:283:- The most common color forms one contiguous horizontal run in every row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:284:- Pixels before those runs share one side color, and pixels after those runs share the other side color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:285:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:286:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:287:- Find the minimum right edge column among the middle-color runs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:288:- In each row, keep the run width and the trailing right-side color count.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:289:- Place the middle-color run so its right edge is at that minimum column, unless the run is too wide, in which case start it at column 0.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:290:- Fill any remaining non-trailing cells with the left-side color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:291:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:292:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:293:The varying row prefixes are movable padding; the stable feature is the leftmost right boundary of the middle-color shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:294:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:295:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:296:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:297:<reference_puzzle index=\"16\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"c803e39c\" lines=\"31-40\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:298:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:299:Expand the second mask into a block grid by stamping the first mask with the two payload colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:300:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:301:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:302:- A background grid has four panels separated by three full-height separator columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:303:- The first two panels contain same-size binary masks; the last two contain solid same-size color squares.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:304:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:305:- Use the second mask as an outer layout. For each foreground cell in that outer mask, place a tile equal to the first mask, coloring its foreground with the first solid-square color and its background with the second solid-square color; outer background cells become all second solid-square color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:306:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:307:- The output is the Kronecker product of the two binary masks, with the two right-hand panel colors providing the palette.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:308:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:309:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:310:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:311:<reference_puzzle index=\"17\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"57edb29d\" lines=\"88-103\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:312:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:313:Extract the single plain rectangle and redraw it with the aligned rectangles' border-relative marker pattern.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:314:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:315:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:316:- The boundary color is the background/separator.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:317:- Foreground objects are dense rectangular regions; exactly one rectangle has only its base color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:318:- Other rectangles contain their base color plus marker pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:319:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:320:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:321:- Crop the only plain rectangle; this crop is the output canvas.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:322:- Use marked rectangles whose row span overlaps the plain rectangle's row span.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:323:- Transfer their marker pixels by preserving each marker run's distance from the nearest rectangle edges.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:324:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:325:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:326:- The marked rectangles are examples of an edge-relative pattern, so the missing plain rectangle receives the same pattern resized to its own dimensions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:327:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:328:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:329:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:330:<reference_puzzle index=\"18\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"2e65ae53\" lines=\"88-103\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:331:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:332:Fill every lattice slot from the color assigned to that slot position by the other lattices.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:333:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:334:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:335:- The background is the dominant color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:336:- The largest foreground color forms several one-pixel-thick rectangular lattice frames.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:337:- The frame lines divide each lattice into the same row-by-column set of rectangular slots; some slots already contain one non-frame color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:338:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:339:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:340:- Infer a color for each logical slot position from the colored slots across all lattice frames.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:341:- Repaint every slot interior in every lattice with the inferred color for its row/column position.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:342:- Keep the frame lines and all background outside frames unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:343:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:344:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:345:- Slot sizes vary by frame, but the complete color pattern is indexed by lattice slot position rather than by absolute pixel size or location.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:346:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:347:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:348:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:349:<reference_puzzle index=\"19\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"182e5d0f\" lines=\"89-103\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:350:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:351:Move each gray marker along its green path until it reaches the cell next to a black-green-black gate, erasing the path behind it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:352:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:353:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:354:- The background is the dominant color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:355:- Foreground components are made from a path color, a paired gate-end color, and single marker pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:356:- A gate is a straight end-center-end motif whose center has the path color and whose two ends share the gate-end color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:357:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:358:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:359:- In every 4-connected foreground component with exactly one marker and one gate, erase the marker and all path-color pixels except the gate center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:360:- Place the marker on the unique path-color pixel adjacent to the gate center but not between the two gate ends.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:361:- Components without both a marker and a gate stay unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:362:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:363:Key insight: The black-green-black motif marks the stopping gate; the gray marker consumes the connected green path until it rests on the path cell immediately beside that gate.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:364:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:365:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:366:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:367:<reference_puzzle index=\"20\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"b71a7747\" lines=\"10-23\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:368:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:369:Extract the hidden two-color image by compacting the rows and columns of its complete mask.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:370:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:371:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:372:The grid contains one pair of colors whose pixels occupy every cell in the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:373:cross product of their active rows and active columns; all other colors form\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:374:the surrounding filler or separators.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:375:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:376:Find that unique color pair, keep exactly the rows and columns touched by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:377:the pair, and return the induced subgrid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:378:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:379:The target image is not chosen by color id; it is the only two-color mask\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:380:whose occupied pixels form a full rectangular row/column product after\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:381:deleting unused rows and columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:382:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:383:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:384:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:385:你的任务：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:386:以参考题为标杆，运用发散性思维进行创新扩展。请发挥创造力，构思全新且巧妙的推理谜题。用中文创造全新的 ARC 谜题描述。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:387:创新方式包括但不限于：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:388:**机制重组**：将多道参考题各自的核心机制提取出来，组合成一个新的多步管道，用到新的场景。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:389:**机制变异**：取几道参考题的核心机制，以机制为基础进行创新并与其他多种机制进行创新重组，使解题路径发生质变而非量变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:390:**逆向构造**：取一道参考题的输出模式，思考\"什么样的输入规则能产生类似的输出结构但需要完全不同的推理过程\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:391:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:392:严格使用下面的 XML 风格格式输出：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:393:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:394:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:395:- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:396:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:397:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:398:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:399:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:400:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:401:请一次性生成 5 个 `<new_puzzle>`，若有较多合适的创新，也可以生成更多，不设上限，但不要输出额外解释。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:402:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:403:注意事项：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:404:1. 任务不应依赖大量先验知识或复杂计算，而应依赖对模式、结构与空间关系的直觉推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:405:2. 关于\"计算\"的边界：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:406:   - **允许使用**（这些都是人类能心算的视觉量）：数像素 / 孔洞 / 对象 / 邻居（≤10 量级）、比大小、按某个可见属性排序、奇偶判断、取最大 / 最小、用一个计数值作为另一个等量几何量（如 N 个像素 → 长度 N 的射线、面积 N → 边长 N）、判断接触 / 相邻 / 包含、粗略中心位置（簇的视觉中点）、\"距离\"作为\"几步\"而不是公式等人类能够直观感受计算的内容。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:407:   - **禁止使用**（这些是算法量而非视觉量，会迫使解题者依赖公式而非视觉直觉）：曼哈顿 / 欧氏 / Chebyshev 距离作为精确查表键、凸包面积、二进制位编码 / 位运算、模运算 / 余数、拓扑距离（BFS / 最短路 / 跳数）、精确几何质心坐标、凸角 / 凹角计数等复杂且不易被看出来的计算都是禁止使用的。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:408:3. 问题必须能从少量示例中推断出来（通常为 3 对训练样例 + 1 个测试样例）。设计时从人类解题者的视觉角度思考：规则涉及的所有关键要素（对象、关系、属性）必须在网格上肉眼可见，不应依赖人眼无法直接观察到的隐含信息（例如颜色id和颜色亮度是禁止使用的）或需要推算的隐藏属性。规则背后的逻辑本身可以有一定挑战性，但解题所需的所有线索必须能从网格中直接获取。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:409:4. 生成的问题描述旨在促进后续用于创建题目网格的代码生成。因此，对输入 / 输出网格的描述以及规则总结必须极其详细；语言风格应易于理解；对于特定对象（如箭头），必须在描述中明确其绘制方式。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:410:5. 描述谜题时避免使用 0 或 1 这类颜色编号；应使用颜色名称，例如 \"red\"。可用颜色如下：Black、Blue、Red、Green、Yellow、Grey、Magenta、Orange、Azure、Maroon。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:411:6. 5 个新题的核心推理机制应明显不同——即从观察样例到归纳规则的认知路径不同，而不仅仅是场景、对象或颜色不同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:412:7. 题目难度应来自机制的隐蔽性而非步骤数。用参考题作为难度标尺——如果你生成的题一个样例就能猜到规则，说明机制太透明，需要加深隐蔽性。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:413:8. 优先从参考题的机制出发进行重组或推演，而非从物理隐喻出发。物理隐喻容易导致大量题目归结为一种模式，例如\"沿方向移动到阻挡处停止\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:414:9. 题目的难度优先来自规则的**结构层数**，而不是单一步骤的复杂度。关于\"结构层数\"的判定标准：**只有解题者需要主动推理才能完成的步骤才算一层**。肉眼一扫即可获得的信息（如\"找到缺口在哪一侧\"、\"数出像素个数\"、\"识别哪个对象最大\"）不构成独立的推理层——它们只是变换的前置输入，不增加认知难度。真正的多层结构是指每一层都需要解题者发现一个非显然的规律。以两层结构为例：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:415:   - ✗ 伪两层：\"找到缺口方向\"→\"把东西推到对面\" — 第一步肉眼可见，实际只有一层推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:416:   - ✓ 真两层：\"通过孔洞数量匹配颜色图例\"→\"用匹配到的颜色重绘对象\" — 两步都需要非平凡的归纳。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:417:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:418:   如果你发现自己写出的题只是\"对每个对象，根据它的某个属性做某变换\"的单步规则，请引入一个需要主动推理的前置步骤。**用堆叠 tie-break 规则或复杂数学公式来\"加难度\"是劣解；用多一层需要归纳的结构嵌套来\"加难度\"才是好解**。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:419:10. 在符合ARC题目和提示词要求的基础上，鼓励尝试创新规则为多层结构的题目，不局限于两层，可以创新三层或四层结构的题目，但不可为了多结构层数违背要求。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:420:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:421:生成后对生成的题执行以下四项审查（审查内容不需要保存到文件）：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:422:1. 原创性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:423:  新题不可与上述参考题相同或类似，不可只是替换颜色、方向、对象类型等表层要素。判断标准：新题的核心推理路径应与任何一道参考题不同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:424:2. 确定性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:425:  规则完全确定，同一输入只能产生唯一输出，每一步操作都有明确定义。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:426:3. 可实现性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:427:  所有必要细节都已给出——对象如何生成、如何识别、如何变换、边界情况如何处理，读完描述后可以直接写代码。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:428:4. ARC 合规性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:429:  网格尺寸合理（≤30×30），使用颜色不超过 10 种，规则复杂度适中，人类能从 3-5 个样例中发现规律。没有使用上述注意事项第二条禁止使用的复杂计算。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/prompt.md:430:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/ids.txt:1:eval/de809cff\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/ids.txt:2:train/b25e450b\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/ids.txt:3:eval/31f7f899\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/ids.txt:4:train/a2d730bd\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/ids.txt:5:train/17829a00\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/ids.txt:6:train/aaecdb9a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/ids.txt:7:train/f0f8a26d\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/ids.txt:8:train/6cbe9eb8\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/ids.txt:9:eval/1ae2feb7\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/ids.txt:10:eval/247ef758\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/ids.txt:11:train/9caf5b84\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/ids.txt:12:train/5587a8d0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/ids.txt:13:train/db7260a4\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/ids.txt:14:eval/88bcf3b4\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/ids.txt:15:train/984d8a3e\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/ids.txt:16:train/c803e39c\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/ids.txt:17:train/57edb29d\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/ids.txt:18:train/2e65ae53\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/ids.txt:19:train/182e5d0f\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/ids.txt:20:train/b71a7747\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:1:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:2:- `description`：根据每个封闭区域内部的色块数量，从色块颜色库中选取对应排位的颜色重新填充该区域的边框。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:3:- `Input structure`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:4:  - 背景为 black。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:5:  - 网格中有若干由 grey 像素围成的封闭矩形边框（边框宽度为1像素），边框内部区域包含数量不等的散落小色块（每个色块为1像素，颜色各异）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:6:  - 网格底部有一行水平排列的颜色样本条：从左到右依次排列若干不同颜色的单像素点，间隔1像素，作为颜色库。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:7:- `Rule`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:8:  - 统计每个 grey 封闭矩形边框内部包含的色块像素数量 N。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:9:  - 在底部颜色库中，从左到右第 N 个颜色即为该边框的目标颜色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:10:  - 将该矩形边框的所有 grey 像素替换为目标颜色；边框内部的色块像素全部清除为 black。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:11:  - 底部颜色库本身保持不变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:12:- `Key insight`：封闭边框内部的色块不是要被保留的内容，而是用来计数的；计数结果作为索引查询底部颜色库，从而决定边框自身的重绘颜色。解题者需要先发现\"内部色块数量\"这一隐含属性，再发现底部色条是按序号查询的颜色映射表。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:13:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:14:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:15:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:16:- `description`：将散落的彩色像素沿其所在行或列的方向聚合到同色 L 形拐角的拐点处，再根据聚合后的像素数决定从拐点延伸的射线长度。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:17:- `Input structure`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:18:  - 背景为 black。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:19:  - 网格中有若干不同颜色的 L 形拐角结构，每个 L 形由两条互相垂直的单像素宽线段组成（一条水平、一条垂直），共享一个拐点像素。每条线段长度至少为2像素（含拐点）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:20:  - 与每个 L 形同色的若干孤立像素散落在网格中，这些孤立像素必定位于 L 形两条臂所在的行或列上（即与某条臂共行或共列）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:21:- `Rule`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:22:  - 对每个 L 形颜色，收集所有同色孤立像素，按照它们与 L 形拐点的行列关系归类：与水平臂同行的归入水平组，与垂直臂同列的归入垂直组。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:23:  - 清除所有孤立像素和原始 L 形。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:24:  - 从拐点出发，沿水平臂的原始延伸方向画一条射线，长度等于水平组的像素数量；沿垂直臂的原始延伸方向画一条射线，长度等于垂直组的像素数量。拐点本身始终保留。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:25:  - 不同颜色的 L 形互不干扰。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:26:- `Key insight`：孤立像素不是装饰，而是通过行列对齐关系分配给 L 形的两条臂的计数器；原始臂长无关紧要，输出臂长完全由收集到的同色孤立像素数量决定。解题者需要先识别行列对齐的归属规则，再发现计数驱动长度的机制。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:27:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:28:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:29:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:30:- `description`：将多个带缺口的矩形框按缺口朝向拼接成链式结构，缺口处用下一个框的颜色填充连接桥。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:31:- `Input structure`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:32:  - 背景为 black。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:33:  - 网格中散布若干不同颜色的空心矩形框（边框宽度为1像素），每个框的某一条边上有一个连续缺口（缺口宽度为2-3像素）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:34:  - 网格角落有一个小型排序提示区：一列从上到下排列的单像素色块，颜色与矩形框一一对应，表示链接顺序。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:35:- `Rule`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:36:  - 按角落提示区从上到下的颜色顺序确定框的链接次序：第1个框为链首，第2个框链接到第1个框，依此类推。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:37:  - 链接方式：将第 k+1 个框平移，使其缺口所在边与第 k 个框的缺口所在边相对（缺口对缺口），两个缺口在同一行或同一列上对齐，框之间留1像素间距。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:38:  - 在两个对齐的缺口之间的间距处，用第 k+1 个框的颜色绘制连接桥（填满缺口宽度 x 1像素的间距）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:39:  - 输出网格裁剪为恰好包含整条链的最小边界框。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:40:- `Key insight`：每个框的缺口不是损坏，而是连接端口；角落色序决定了拼接顺序，而缺口朝向决定了空间排列方向。解题者需要先从角落提示发现排列顺序，再理解缺口作为定向连接器的拼接规则，最后发现连接桥的颜色取自被链接框而非链接到的框。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:41:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:42:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:43:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:44:- `description`：识别网格中重叠放置的多个透明色层，根据层叠遮挡关系还原每层的完整原始形状，然后将各层按面积从小到大水平排列输出。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:45:- `Input structure`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:46:  - 背景为 black。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:47:  - 网格中有若干不同颜色的矩形区域发生了部分重叠。在重叠区域，后放置的颜色完全覆盖先放置的颜色，因此某些矩形仅有部分像素可见（呈现为 L 形、U 形或其他被遮挡后的残留形状）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:48:  - 每种前景颜色恰好对应一个矩形（非框，是实心矩形）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:49:  - 没有颜色被完全遮挡（每种颜色至少有1个像素可见）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:50:- `Rule`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:51:  - 对每种前景颜色，根据其可见像素推断出该颜色原始完整矩形的尺寸：可见像素的行范围即矩形的行跨度，列范围即矩形的列跨度。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:52:  - 还原每个颜色的完整实心矩形。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:53:  - 按矩形面积从小到大排序。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:54:  - 在输出网格中，将这些还原的矩形从左到右水平排列，矩形之间间隔1列 black，所有矩形顶部对齐于第0行。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:55:- `Key insight`：被遮挡的矩形虽然不完整，但其可见像素的行列范围已足够还原完整尺寸——这利用了矩形的轴对齐特性。解题者需要先认识到每种颜色对应一个被遮挡的完整矩形，再发现从残留像素的边界范围可以还原原始形状，最后按面积排列输出。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:56:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:57:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:58:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:59:- `description`：网格中的每个彩色种子像素沿其所在象限对应的对角方向生长出与同象限内壁面距离等长的 L 形枝条，枝条颜色由种子与中心标记的相对位置决定。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:60:- `Input structure`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:61:  - 背景为 black。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:62:  - 网格正中央有一个 red 十字标记（1像素宽，横竖各占满整行整列），将网格分为四个象限（左上、右上、左下、右下）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:63:  - 每个象限内散布若干孤立的彩色种子像素（颜色不为 red 或 black），每个象限内的种子颜色相同但不同象限的种子颜色可能不同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:64:  - 网格边缘有 grey 边框（1像素宽）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:65:- `Rule`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:66:  - 每个种子像素根据所在象限确定生长方向：左上象限向左上生长，右上象限向右上生长，左下象限向左下生长，右下象限向右下生长。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:67:  - 生长方式：从种子出发，先沿水平方向（朝象限外侧边框方向）画一条线段，长度等于种子到该方向 grey 边框的像素距离减1；再从该线段末端沿垂直方向（朝象限外侧边框方向）画一条线段，长度等于种子到该方向 grey 边框的像素距离减1。两段构成 L 形。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:68:  - L 形枝条使用种子自身的颜色绘制。种子像素本身保留。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:69:  - red 十字标记和 grey 边框保持不变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:70:  - 枝条不会越过 red 十字线或 grey 边框。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:71:- `Key insight`：red 十字将空间划分为四个独立象限，每个象限的生长方向由其相对于中心的位置隐含决定；枝条的两段长度不是固定的，而是由种子到边框的距离动态决定。解题者需要先理解十字线的象限划分作用，再发现每个种子的 L 形生长方向和长度都取决于其在象限中的空间位置。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:72:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:73:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:74:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:75:- `description`：在包含多个相同模板图案副本的网格中，找出每个副本相对于\"标准版\"的差异像素，将所有差异像素叠加到一个干净的模板上生成输出。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:76:- `Input structure`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:77:  - 背景为 black。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:78:  - 网格中以规则间距排列着若干个大小相同的矩形区域（如 2x3 或 3x4 的网格排列），每个区域包含一个近似相同的多色图案。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:79:  - 这些图案副本大部分像素相同，但每个副本有少量像素（1-3个）与其他副本不同——即被\"篡改\"过。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:80:  - 存在一个\"多数一致\"的标准图案：对于每个像素位置，多数副本在该位置的颜色即为标准颜色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:81:- `Rule`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:82:  - 通过多数投票确定每个像素位置的标准颜色，得到标准模板。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:83:  - 对每个副本，找出与标准模板不同的像素位置及其篡改颜色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:84:  - 创建一个与模板大小相同的输出网格，以标准模板为底，将所有副本的所有差异像素叠加上去（差异像素的颜色覆盖标准颜色）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:85:  - 如果多个副本在同一位置都有差异，取最后一个副本（按从左到右、从上到下的阅读顺序）的差异颜色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:86:- `Key insight`：多个\"几乎相同\"的副本不是冗余，而是通过差异编码了隐藏信息；解题者需要先通过对比发现\"多数一致即为标准\"的投票机制，再收集每个副本偏离标准的\"异常\"像素，最后将这些异常合并到一个模板上。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:87:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:88:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:89:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:90:- `description`：将网格中每条彩色路径按照路径上遇到的关卡标记依次截断并变色，形成分段渐变的彩色路径。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:91:- `Input structure`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:92:  - 背景为 black。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:93:  - 网格中有若干条由 grey 像素构成的单像素宽连续路径（4-连通），路径不分叉，两端各有一个端点像素。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:94:  - 每条路径的起点端（一端）标记为 blue 像素（替代该位置的 grey）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:95:  - 路径上间隔分布着若干 red 像素作为关卡标记（替代该位置的 grey）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:96:  - 网格边缘有一个颜色序列参考条：从左到右排列若干不同颜色的像素（不含 black、grey、blue、red），表示分段着色的颜色顺序。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:97:- `Rule`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:98:  - 从每条路径的 blue 端点出发，沿路径行走。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:99:  - 将 blue 端点到第一个 red 关卡之间的所有像素（含 blue 端点，不含 red 关卡）重新着色为颜色序列的第1个颜色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:100:  - 将第1个 red 关卡到第2个 red 关卡之间的像素（含第1个关卡，不含第2个关卡）着色为颜色序列的第2个颜色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:101:  - 依此类推，每经过一个关卡，使用颜色序列中的下一个颜色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:102:  - 最后一个 red 关卡到路径另一端之间的像素（含最后的关卡和端点）使用序列中的下一个颜色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:103:  - 颜色序列参考条在输出中保持不变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:104:- `Key insight`：grey 路径和 red 关卡在输出中完全消失，被分段颜色取代；解题者需要先识别 blue 为起点、red 为分割标记的角色分工，再发现边缘颜色条提供了分段着色的顺序映射，最后理解路径遍历方向决定了颜色分配。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/16/des.md:105:</new_puzzle>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
